## Why This Is Asked
This checks practical CV setup, leakage awareness, and model selection on small data.

## Key Concepts
- Data leakage prevention
- Stratified cross-validation
- Pipeline preprocessing
- Model comparison metrics (AUROC, calibration)

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: stratified K-fold CV in JS-like syntax
const k = 5;
const folds = stratifiedKFoldSplit(labels, k);
for (const [trainIdx, testIdx] of folds) {
  const model = trainLogisticRegression(features[trainIdx], labels[trainIdx]);
  const preds = model.predictProba(features[testIdx]);
  console.log(rocAuc(labels[testIdx], preds));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle class imbalance if AUROC is similar across models?
- How could you incorporate feature engineering without leaking future information?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical domain adaptation for multimodal models under edge latency constraints; evaluates PEFT decisions, data strategy, and evaluation protocols.

## Key Concepts
- Multimodal alignment
- Domain adaptation with limited labels
- PEFT (Adapters/LoRA)
- Inference acceleration on edge
- Evaluation metrics for cross-domain retrieval

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: apply LoRA adapters to a pretrained transformer
const model = loadModel('fashion_multimodal_base');
const adapters = loadAdapters('fashion_lora');
model.applyAdapters(adapters);
model.train(fashionDataset, {
  loss: 'supervisedContrastive',
  batchSize: 32,
  epochs: 10
});
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests system design for real-time fraud scoring at scale with privacy constraints, multi-tenant data sharing, and safe rollbacks.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming feature store and time-window features
- Hybrid inference paths: server-side and on-device
- Federated learning with differential privacy
- Drift detection and canary-based rollout strategies
- Model calibration and per-transaction explainability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo scoring sketch
function score(tx, globalModel, localModel){
  const feats = extract(tx)
  const s1 = globalModel.predict(feats)
  const s2 = localModel.predict(feats)
  return calibrate((0.6*s1 + 0.4*s2));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle label latency for online updates?
- What metrics trigger rollback and how would you test rollbacks?
